{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And on your new moons.</b> Rabbi Moses the Kohen the Sephardi, of blessed memory, said that its meaning is the month of Nisan, for thus it is written, \"it is first for you,\" and afterward it says, \"this is the burnt-offering of the new moon in its month\" — that they shall do so in every month; therefore he added \"for the months of the year,\" and his interpretation is correct, even though one could object regarding the yod in ובראשי חדשיכם, only because we find הנה חדש מחר, his statement is straightforward."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:19:44.783028197Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}